# M / B011 — dependency-injection, development-workflow, docker.

C R184 OL GOV-002 | MUST | For a new application or a substantial feature read SPECIFICATION.md (and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md) before planning or implementing. | new applications and substantial features | none stated
C R185 OL GOV-018 | MUST | If a request looks questionable, identify the concrete concern and raise it with an alternative before implementing; this never permits silently rewriting or ignoring the user's requirement. | requests | none stated
C R186 OL PST-008 | MUST | Whenever a Domain or persistence change affects seeded entities (new required or removed/renamed properties, changed relationships, new required related entities, changed enum/status values, new states, changed invariants) update DbSeeder in the same change so recreating the Development database yields valid representative data; review DbSeeder together with migrations that change seeded entities. | seed data co-change | Already seeded rows of an existing database are not patched.
C R187 OL PST-010 | MUST | Treat EF Core migrations as source code: review every generated migration before committing it (destructive schema changes, unexpected column recreation, data migrations, indexes, foreign keys, delete behavior). | EF Core migrations | none stated
C R188 OL RUN-012 | MUST | A performance-motivated change identifies the actual bottleneck or cost, preserves observable behavior, uses the simplest optimization that addresses it, adds or preserves tests for affected behavior and benchmarks or profiles non-obvious or complex optimizations. | performance changes | none stated
C R189 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run code-review (or the code-reviewer agent) and address the findings before final verification. | substantial work | none stated
C R190 OL WF-005,WF-006 | MUST | Verify Docker changes by building the image and verifying application startup, required ports and configuration, non-root behavior when relevant and health-probe integration, reviewing the image for accidental secrets or files, and running meaningful application tests. | Docker changes | none stated
C X17 EX WF-009 | MUST | The development-workflow output reports what changed, Delegated choices worth noting, unresolved Decision Requests, the verify report and every change-specific obligation that was not applicable with the reason. | implementation reports | none stated | WF-009 requires truthful verification reporting and GOV-017 reporting of unresolved Decision Requests; no oracle policy requires reporting delegated choices or non-applicable obligations. | A completion report that omits why the seed-data obligation did not apply does not follow the workflow.

